# ntfsplus: the author's standalone packaging of NTFSPLUS, the read/write NTFS
# driver Linux carries as fs/ntfs. The ogc kernel builds it off
# (CONFIG_NTFS_FS unset), so the image has no ntfs.ko of its own; it ships
# under updates/ and never loads on its own (55-ntfsplus.sh).
URL=https://github.com/namjaejeon/linux-ntfs.git
# Pinned on purpose, and to a merge commit of main only: ntfs-next is
# force-pushed and its tip may be mid-rework. A bump needs the runtime mount
# proof on a booted target kernel, because vermagic and modinfo pass on a
# module whose breakage is a runtime mismatch (docs/gotchas.md).
COMMIT=d6d09e6f017f45aae062e05e64301f43a2c66ea1
# The Makefile emits ntfs.ko and the driver registers the filesystem type
# "ntfs": "ntfsplus" is the project's name, never the module's or the mount
# type's.
KO_NAME=ntfs
# `make -C <kernel> M=<clone> modules` leaves the object at the clone root
# (Makefile: obj-$(CONFIG_NTFS_FS) += ntfs.o).
KO_BUILD_PATH=ntfs.ko
# That fragment is gated on the kernel's own symbol: against a kernel that
# leaves CONFIG_NTFS_FS unset it expands to `obj- += ntfs.o`, kbuild compiles
# nothing and exits 0. Forcing the symbol on the make line is what makes the
# module build at all (docs/gotchas.md).
KO_BUILD_ARGS=CONFIG_NTFS_FS=m
# No MODULE_VERSION in the source: nothing to assert.
KO_VERSION=
